      "curator_note": "Lower branch of Equation 8.56, on the reaction arrow labelled 'alpha' leaving the ring-opened distonic ion .CH2CH2CH2CH2-O+=CH2: radical-site alpha-cleavage in which the tail radical (C3) forms the C3=C4 pi bond and the C4-C5 bond breaks, expelling neutral ethylene (printed to the left of the product as 'C2H4 +') and leaving the distonic oxonium ion .CH2CH2-O+=CH2 at m/z 58, 1%. Book draws 0 arcs for THIS branch: the two arcs visible on the m/z 58 structure belong to its subsequent step (encoded separately as IMS8-EQ8.56e), so all three fishhooks encoded here are curator-supplied for electron balance."
    },
