      "support_type": "curator_inferred",
      "locator": {"page": 182, "equation": "8.56", "figure": null, "panel": null, "section": null},
      "confidence": null,
      "curator_note": "rule_index.json 'by_equation' has no entry for 8.56; no MØD rule variable is cross-linked to this scheme. This is the six-membered-ring (tetrahydropyran) analogue of the four-/five-membered-ring branch encoded as IMS8-EQ8.50 (Eq. 8.50, p. 178), which uses the same three-fishhook radical-site alpha-cleavage pattern. The species undergoing this step is the ring-opened isomer of the molecular ion (C5H10O+., m/z 86), so adduct is kept as [M]+•. The page prints abundances as bare percentages without naming the experiment; they are the book's standard 70 eV EI values."
